      "message": "the suggestion proposed by gemini does not make sense\n\n```\nLOG_ERR() in plat_free() routes through Zephyr\u0027s logging subsystem (LOG_MODULE_REGISTER(egis630_pal, LOG_LEVEL_INF)), not through the custom output_log() hook that writes to printf_buffer.\n```\n\n```\n[00:00:00.240,000] \u003cerr\u003e egis630_pal: Error - plat_free called with NULL double pointer.\nThe message was printed directly by Zephyr\u0027s logger, so printf_buffer remained empty (\\0), causing strstr() to return NULL.\n```",
